# The build context is the repository root (both Dockerfiles need the
# workspace files). An allowlist: only the workspace manifests, the lockfile,
# apps/ and the one package the API runs with (audit-contract) reach the
# builder, minus the files below. Anything else placed under them (a database
# dump, say) would still reach the build stage and its cache: keep such files
# out of the repository tree. The final images get only what their
# Dockerfiles copy.
*
!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!tsconfig.base.json
!apps/
!packages/audit-contract/

# Inside them: host installs, build output, logs, and secrets in their usual
# file forms stay out.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/dist-dev
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.log
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
**/.envrc
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.jks
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ecdsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/*.dump
apps/api/src/prisma/generated

.examples/
